              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "s3t3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Do you have the drive to have a productive, rewarding career with better training, better pay and better benefits? The McCoy Group has locations across the United States with openings for medium and heavy-duty truck and trailer technicians. Whether you are already an expert diesel tech or just getting started, we have a career path for you.",
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s3t4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Diesel Technicians are highly-respected technical experts in their field. They inspect, repair and maintain the tough diesel engines and computerized management systems found in large trucks, construction equipment, dump trucks and more. Diesel technicians work independently to solve problems using professional judgment and take responsibility for the safe operation of the equipment that they repair and maintain.",
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "s3t5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We are also very proud of our partnership with the Department of Defense (DoD) Skillbridge Program, which provides active-duty service members with hands-on training in diesel technology. The Department of Defense (DoD) Skillbridge program is a program that enables transitioning service members to gain valuable civilian work experience through internships, apprenticeships, and industry training during their final 180 days of service, connecting them with industry partners for real-world job experiences.",
                    "width": "full"
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "paddingTop": 0,
                      "paddingBottom": 0
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
